# London Parkour Google stack — read / write

Paid **class bookings** are the outcome. Do not invent metrics. Never print
private keys, service-account JSON, or app passwords.

**Reads:** allowed. **Writes:** only after an explicit user request naming the
change. `validate_only` / dry-run first, then mutate, then re-read and report
IDs. Do not raise spend, scopes, or publish to Live unless asked.

Shared identity: Cloud project `cursor-to-gtm`, SA
`cursor-to-gtm@cursor-to-gtm.iam.gserviceaccount.com`, key file
`~/.config/google-ads/service-account.json`. Same SA is in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`
for GTM (env JSON) and GSC (key file). Never dump those files.

Call `GetDynamicTools` on a namespace before the first tool in a session.

## Google Ads

| | |
|---|---|
| Customer | `8689582919` (UI `868-958-2919`) |
| Conversion ID | `AW-810152772` — **not** the customer ID |
| Read | MCP `user-google-ads` (official, **read-only**) |
| Write | Python `~/.config/google-ads/venv/bin/python` + YAML `~/.config/google-ads/google-ads.yaml` |
| API | v25+. Explorer on the Cloud project. Ads UI role Standard |
| Skill | `.cursor/skills/google-ads/` |

MCP: `customers_list_accessible_customers` → `metadata_get_resource_metadata`
before each new `resource` → `search_search` with `customer_id`, `resource`,
`fields[]`. Optional `conditions`, `orderings`, `limit`. **Never** pass a raw
GAQL `query` string to MCP.

Writes: `validate_only=True` first. Do not hardcode `v24`. Do not set
`target_spend_micros` (overrides daily budget). Empty bidding oneofs are no-ops
— set a real field (e.g. `target_spend.cpc_bid_ceiling_micros`). RSA
`final_urls` / headlines: `AdService.mutate_ads`, not `AdGroupAdService` UPDATE.
Some conversion actions are API-immutable (hide/remove in the Ads UI).

Explorer cannot: billing, user-admin, Keyword/Reach Plan, `CreateCustomerClient`.

Fallback if MCP is down: Python `GoogleAdsService.search_stream` in
`.cursor/skills/google-ads/write.md` (**search only** unless the user asked
for a mutate).

## Google Tag Manager

